{"id":"20260827T023808.704014167Z-66c2bcd7","time":"2026-08-27T02:38:08.704014167Z","session_id":"session-20260827T023430.725711425Z","task_id":"task-1787798070725908072","source":"system","kind":"status","summary":"Authority for this plan, by lane.\n\nrequested objective:\n  semaphore.Weighted.TryAcquire and Acquire duplicate the decision about whether a request can proceed immediately. Factor that decision into one place so the two paths cannot diverge, with no change to observable behaviour.\n  NOT established as a human objective — submitted unattended; no human presence was established\n  the wording is the task; it is not a person's authorization for it\n\ntechnical claims:\n  [evidence-bearing] Weighted.Acquire and Weighted.TryAcquire currently evaluate the identical predicate s.size-s.cur \u003e= n \u0026\u0026 s.waiters.Len() == 0 while holding s.mu. (semaphore/semaphore.go: Weighted.Acquire and Weighted.TryAcquire) — source: repository\n  [evidence-bearing] Both immediate-success paths increment s.cur by n only after that predicate succeeds. (semaphore/semaphore.go: Weighted.Acquire and Weighted.TryAcquire) — source: repository\n  [evidence-bearing] Acquire checks for an already-done context after locking and before evaluating immediate eligibility, while TryAcquire has no context behavior. (semaphore/semaphore.go: Weighted.Acquire and Weighted.TryAcquire) — source: repository\n  [evidence-bearing] The no-waiters condition preserves queue fairness; notifyWaiters documents that bypassing an unsatisfied front waiter could starve large requests. (semaphore/semaphore.go: Weighted.notifyWaiters) — source: repository\n  [evidence-bearing] Existing tests cover immediate Acquire and TryAcquire outcomes, already-canceled Acquire behavior, oversized requests, and starvation-sensitive queue behavior. (semaphore/semaphore_test.go) — source: repository\n  [evidence-bearing] Scoped Sensei preflight classifies the change as LOW_RISK with local blast radius and no approval gate, while reporting no directly anchored governing rule. (semaphore/semaphore.go) — source: graph\n  [evidence-bearing] Sensei identifies the semaphore public API contract only as a candidate, not active governing authority. (contract:contract.library_api.semaphore) — source: graph\n  the objective does not establish any of these. Evidence does.\n\nconsequence decision:\n  BOUNDED — the candidate worktree: files are edited in an isolated checkout, the diff is audited before it leaves, and discarding the worktree leaves the world unchanged\n  assessed from the action, not from who asked and not from whether the plan satisfies the objective.\n\nrouted: bounded-knowledge-gap\n"}
